        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Stanley Elkin, Anne Lamott\n- Works: Mrs. Ted Bliss\n- Companies: Hyperion Books\n- Topics: American fiction, satire, consumerism, popular culture, male-female relations\n\nFacts:\n- Stanley Elkin was born on May 11, 1930, and he was an American novelist, short story writer, and essayist.\n- Anne Lamott was born on April 10, 1954, and she is an American novelist and non-fiction writer.\n- Stanley Elkin's extravagant, satirical fiction revolved around American consumerism, popular culture, and male-female relations.\n- In 1995, Stanley Elkin died on May 31.\n- Mrs. Ted Bliss is a 1995 novel by American author Stanley Elkin.\n- Hyperion Books published Mrs. Ted Bliss.",
